🚀 Day 26/90 – GitHub CLI (gh) Basics

Today I learned how to use GitHub CLI (gh) to manage GitHub directly from the terminal.

What I practiced:

✅ Installed GitHub CLI (gh) ✅ Logged into GitHub using gh auth login ✅ Created a new GitHub repository from the terminal ✅ Created and viewed GitHub Issues ✅ Closed an Issue using CLI ✅ Created a feature branch ✅ Pushed code to GitHub ✅ Learned why a Pull Request can fail when branches don't share a common history

Key Commands:

gh auth login
gh repo create
gh repo view
gh issue create
gh issue list
gh issue close
gh pr create

What I learned:

GitHub CLI helps developers perform GitHub tasks without opening the browser. It saves time and is very useful in DevOps automation.
Every error taught me something new, and debugging those errors improved my understanding of Git and GitHub.

